proposals.evidence:
Same mechanism as proposal 1: the corner metric pulls the second tower along the home's own edge. Forward second towers stand 432-467 from that edge and 479-556 forward, against 594-610 and 357-383 in back-contact races. Example, game 917848042 (home bottom-right): at t12 the corner anchor took site 0 (628 forward) for the first tower. The back-edge anchor (1769,650) takes site 7 (340): 354 away, against 517 for site 0.
Counterfactual at the first ladder walk to a second or later tower in [release, contact):
- 15 of 19 lost forward targets change; contact 517 -> 373; beyond 406: 19 -> 6;
- walks 289 -> 348, shorter than proposal 1's 394;
- won forward races: 483 -> 326;
- back races: 5 of 10 lost and 4 of 26 won targets change;
- all races: median contact distance 406 -> 317; beyond 406: 53 -> 28 of 106.
It never runs out of targets, unlike proposal 1 (41 of 106 races have at most one site within 450 left at the contact), so it has no ladder stall and no idle top-up phase. The expected local first-wave shift is about the same as proposal 1's: median about 320-340, merges about 15 %.
